      "value": "@{5f3a1667c9dbb86d5b647895|full_name}: Yea i see, the asset files do contain all necessary data (and a ID link to the necessary base script) i just looked into one. I'm just not sure if a script could read these values out of a scene object when its missing, it might need to be turned into a prefab but even that would still be better.\nBut like i said, unless they massively improve the auto conversion which currently is a massive hit-or-miss due to the many wonky and hacky solutions people came up over the years you might want to start from scratch anyway even if the conversion doesn't totally break it, it will only net you very very basic translated phys bones at best, you will have to go in and tweak them regardless so ultimately an outside auto conversion is somewhat useless beyond a very very marginal time save if at all.\nI'd say this is a very minor nice to have if at all but ultimately a waste of time (they have much more pressing issues to fix) which is most likely going to get deprecated at some point anyway (possibly only leaving the VRChat internal auto conversion option if that one isn't removed either with the phase out of dynamic bones)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
